rYnShqbxoHilSo0filhhQvQ.jpg","video":"","hasVideo":false},{"id":"1231","date":"2026-11-08T19:20:29+00:00","text":"On the Verge pinned a photo","image":"","video":"","hasVideo":false},{"id":"1230","date":"2026-11-08T19:20:24+00:00","text":"What's coming · Nov 9 – Nov 15 Take-Two opens the week with its last earnings call before GTA VI lands on Nov 19. Then the AI money talks: CoreWeave and Cisco report, and Lisbon hosts Web Summit. Mon Nov 9: Take-Two reports fiscal Q2 after the close – it's the last call before GTA VI ships on Nov 19. Any wobble on that date and the stock moves first, questions later. Mon Nov 9: Web Summit opens in Lisbon and runs through Thu Nov 12 – about 70,000 people expected. Lots of AI agent pitches, a few keynotes worth clipping. Tue Nov 10: CoreWeave reports Q3, call at 5pm ET – the GPU cloud is a live read on how much AI compute people actually rent. Watch the backlog and whether data center buildouts are on time. Tue Nov 10: Football Manager 27 comes out on PC, Mac, PS5 and Xbox Series X|S. FM26 got a mixed reception last year, so this one has to win the regulars back. Tue Nov 10: Adobe MAX starts in Miami Beach, through Thu Nov 12 – Adobe's yearly drop of Firefly and Creative Cloud features. See how far the AI tools go into Photoshop and Premiere. Thu Nov 12: Metaphor: ReFantazio arrives on Switch 2 – Atlus's 2024 RPG, one of that year's best-reviewed games, finally portable. Thu Nov 12: Cisco reports fiscal Q1 after the close – it guided to $18.0B–$18.2B in revenue. AI networking orders from the big clouds are the number that matters. See it coming.","image":"https://cdn4.telesco.pe/file/i0hJMDXQelmjFSRG-BdW0OSy1vcmktHvVK0-dgltF9Nnsa8OkUyxgBfaONmPkzknoU02nCmHRFS6EFNDzjqYiednUFH3-dOlFR9Ib77QRx5gMFUtEw01loxgfBex4c90ehtOXN6P9mSYB8YDh13rCWl8TgaZqg5DefbeA6EFWnwZGaa214FbZZwthN8q4G8qU2N1J9_ZzcmLA2RQAG1dnLO_AyD6Zj4hPRa1clqPZosWWjf1JG0MokD5iVFcR7CtxRTt8dQWlRj52xcr1P1EHijyNOR3YueO6dPZn37TmfMdgZ4trX7C8cke6oblmUujBc9B2DUM8HkUKEacST8RxQ.jpg","video":